"""Deli Counter 0.249.0 (the factory's roadmap 283): a room holds what stands on its storey, and the shelter pass runs
over the library.

`_room_has_cover`, `_room_has_shelter` and `combat_audit._cover_in_room` each asked a piece's storey their own way --
the first two the float window 0.246.0 closed in furnish's count, the audit `abs(z - floor) < sh` on a volume's centre,
which counted everything standing on the floor below as cover in the room over it -- and none asked a marker's.
`level_design.stands_on_storey` and `marker_on_storey` are the one test now, asked by all four. Attributing every room
that fills found the second defect: nothing ran the shelter pass over the library (`enrich` runs in `presets.make`,
`build.py` builds a spec as it stands), so eleven library combat rooms had nothing to fight from. `migrate_shelter.py`
fills them; a test keeps the library a fixed point of the pass.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has
been worked out: `level_design.py` and `combat_audit.py` (anchored hunks); the nine refurnished specs, carried whole;
the new `test_storey_shelter.py` and `migrate_shelter.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a
proven clone (`patches/dc_storey_shelter/gen_dc_storey_shelter.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte,
a second run refused (`patches/dc_storey_shelter/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_storey_shelter.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
